  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A boy of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is standing on a piece of wood having mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>. If the coefficient of friction between the wood and the floor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the maximum force that the boy can exert on the rope so that the piece of wood does not move from its place is _______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. (Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p><p>[Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0098_5ff801902010.png\" style=\"width: 421px; height: 277px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "30",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0098_ea2bdb54fcd4.png\" style=\"width: 203px; height: 197px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p>"
  }
